course: dictionary
lesson: 4986
title: The index: finding things fast
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: An index is a list that helps you find things quickly. In a non-fiction book, it is the alphabetical list at the back, with page numbers next to each topic. «you find facts with ... non-fiction books and their index» means you can look up a topic like volcanoes and go straight to the right page, without reading the whole book.
explain: Index is also a word for a finger. The index finger is the one next to your thumb, the one you use for pointing. The same word can mean different things, so read the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: In maths, index (plural indices) means the small raised number that shows a power. In 5², the 2 is the index: it tells you to multiply 5 by itself, so 5² = 5 × 5 = 25. Index can also be a verb: to index a book means to make a list of its topics.
fact: An index is an alphabetical list at the back of a book, with page numbers.
fact: Using the index is a shortcut: you find a topic fast instead of turning every page.
fact: The index finger is the finger next to the thumb, used for pointing.
fact: In maths, an index (plural indices) is a small raised number that shows a power, like the 2 in 5².
fact: «Look it up in the index» means check that list to find the right page.
exercise: For a project, where do you look to find the page for volcanoes in a non-fiction book? | The author's photo | The first page of the first chapter | The cover of the book | *The index at the back of the book
exercise: In 5², what does the small raised 2 show? | A price that has gone up | The number of pages in the book | *A power, telling you to multiply 5 by itself | The finger you point with
exercise: Which finger is the index finger? | The middle finger | *The finger next to the thumb | The little finger | The thumb
test: What does «index» mean in «Check the index to find page 45»? | A finger for pointing | A price that has gone up | A raised number in maths | *A list at the back of a book with page numbers
test: In 2³, what does the 3 show, and what is 2³? | A price: 2 × 3 = 6 | A page number: 2 × 3 = 6 | *A power: 2 × 2 × 2 = 8 | A finger: 2 + 3 = 5
exam: What is the main use of an index in a non-fiction book? | Decorating the cover | Counting the words in the book | Showing the author's photo | *Finding a topic quickly, with its page numbers
